hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16048","Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash narrated to us, he said, Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Hassan al-Bakri, he said, we came to Madinah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon the pulpit, and Bilal was standing before him, wearing a sword before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and there were black banners, and I asked, what are these banners, and they said, Amr ibn al-As has come from a raid."
"16049","Affan narrated to us, he said, Sallam Abu al-Mundhir narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wail, from al-Harith ibn Hassan, he said, I passed by an old woman at al-Rabadhah, stranded, of Banu Tamim. He said, so she said, where do you intend, he said, so I said, we intend the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). She said, so carry me with you, for I have a need to him. He said, so I said, so I entered the mosque, and it was crowded with people, and a black banner was fluttering, and I said, what is the affair of the people today, they said, this is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) intending to send Amr ibn al-As forth. He said, so I said, O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to make al-Dahna a barrier between us and Banu Tamim, do so, for it was once ours. He said, so the old woman started up, and zeal seized her, and she said, O Messenger of Allah, where do you force your Mudar. I said, O Messenger of Allah, I carried this one, and I did not feel that she would be an opponent to me. He said, I said, I seek refuge with Allah from being as the first said. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, and what did the first say. He said, you have fallen upon the expert. Sallam says, this is a fool, the Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) says, you have fallen upon the expert. He said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tell on, seeking to draw out the story from him. He said, Ad sent their delegate Qayl, and he alighted upon Muawiyah ibn Bakr for a month, he giving him wine to drink, and the two locusts singing to him, and he went until he came upon the mountains of Mahrah, and said, O Allah, I did not come for a captive to ransom, nor for a sick one to treat, so give drink to Your servant as You used to give, and give Muawiyah ibn Bakr drink for a month, he thanking him for the wine he drank with him. He said, so black clouds passed, and it was called out, take it as ashes, dusty ashes, leaving none of Ad. Abu Wail said, so it reached me that what was sent upon them of wind was like what runs in a ring."
"16050","Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, he said, Abu al-Mundhir Sallam ibn Sulayman al-Nahwi narrated to me, he said, Asim ibn Abi al-Nujud narrated to us, from Abu Wail, from al-Harith ibn Yazid al-Bakri, he said, I went out to complain of al-Ala ibn al-Hadrami to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I passed by al-Rabadhah, and there was an old woman of Banu Tamim, stranded, and she said to me, O servant of Allah, I have a need to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), will you convey me to him. He said, so I carried her, and I came to Madinah, and the mosque was crowded with its people, and a black banner was fluttering, and Bilal was wearing a sword before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I said, what is the affair of the people, they said, he intends to send Amr ibn al-As forth. He said, so I sat. He said, so he entered his house, or he said, his lodging, and I sought permission upon him, and he permitted me, and I entered and greeted, and he said: Was there anything between you and Banu Tamim. He said, so I said: Yes. He said, and victory was ours over them, and I passed by an old woman of Banu Tamim, stranded, and she asked me to carry her to you, and here she is at the door, so he permitted her, and she entered, and I said, O Messenger of Allah, if you see fit to make between us and Banu Tamim a barrier, make al-Dahna. So the old woman became zealous and started up, she said, O Messenger of Allah, then where do you force your Mudar. He said, I said, my parable is but what the first said, a goat that carried its death, I carried this one, and I did not feel that she was an opponent to me, I seek refuge with Allah and His Messenger from being like the delegate of Ad. He said: Tell on, and what is the delegate of Ad, and he knows the story better than him, but he seeks to draw it out. I said, Ad suffered drought, so they sent a delegate of theirs called Qayl, and he passed by Muawiyah ibn Bakr, and stayed with him a month, he giving him wine to drink, and two slavegirls called the two locusts singing to him, and when the month passed, he went out to the mountains of Tihamah, and called, O Allah, You know that I did not come to a sick one to treat, nor to a captive to ransom, O Allah, give Ad drink as You used to give. So black clouds passed by him, and it was called from them, choose. So he pointed to a black cloud of them, and it was called from it, take it as ashes, dusty ashes, leaving none of Ad. He said, so it did not reach me that there was sent upon them of wind except what runs in this ring of mine, until they perished. Abu Wail said, and he spoke truth. He said, so when a woman and a man would send a delegate of theirs, they would say, do not be like the delegate of Ad."
